id: pmc-kdm1
title: "Docstring coverage gate: a parser-backed, self-scanning mandatory check"
description: "Fail the build when any documented-surface declaration lacks a real docstring. The gate parses each file into a syntax tree rather than scanning text, so a JSDoc inside a string literal or above a commented-out declaration cannot satisfy it, and it rejects a comment that merely restates the identifier. It walks its roots instead of reading a file list, so a new file is covered the moment it exists, and it fails rather than passing when a root is missing or empty."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: "area:quality",docs,gate
created_at: "2026-08-02T07:33:51.652Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-02T07:34:39.928Z"
deadline: "2026-08-31T00:00:00.000Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-02T07:34:39.914Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-02T07:34:39.914Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "npm run docstring exits 0 across src and scripts; exits 1 naming file:line:symbol for a missing, too-short, or name-restating docstring; a declaration inside a string or a comment is never counted; a missing or empty root fails; the gate passes on its own source"
resolution: "Parser-backed gate enforcing exported declarations, non-private class members, and functions over 4 body lines"
expected_result: "A gate that cannot be satisfied by a JSDoc in a string, a comment, or a name restatement"
actual_result: Gate passes on src and scripts; 103 real violations found and fixed
